From: Haiku Pi port
Subject: wsi: pass Mesa's Haiku view surface info on to the driver

Haiku has no registered Vulkan surface extension; Mesa's Haiku WSI takes the
BView of a surface as a VkHaikuSurfaceCreateInfoMESA chained to
VkHeadlessSurfaceCreateInfoEXT (Mesa's <vulkan/vk_haiku_surface.h>). The loader
copies a surface's create info for the drivers' lazily created surfaces and
leaves out the whole chain when it holds a struct it does not know, so it must
know this one.

--- a/loader/wsi.c
+++ b/loader/wsi.c
@@ -1486,6 +1486,11 @@
 
     const struct loader_struct_type_info ci_types[] = {
         {VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_HEADLESS_SURFACE_CREATE_INFO_EXT, sizeof(VkHeadlessSurfaceCreateInfoEXT)},
+#if defined(__HAIKU__)
+        // Mesa's Haiku view surfaces: a VkHaikuSurfaceCreateInfoMESA in the chain (Mesa's
+        // <vulkan/vk_haiku_surface.h>; sType, pNext, flags, the BView)
+        {(VkStructureType)1000256900, sizeof(VkHeadlessSurfaceCreateInfoEXT) + sizeof(void *)},
+#endif
     };
     copy_surface_create_info(loader_inst, icd_surface, pCreateInfo, sizeof(ci_types) / sizeof(ci_types[0]), ci_types,
                              "VkHeadlessSurfaceCreateInfoEXT", pAllocator);
